Tank Level Indicator Water level sensors are placed inside the water tank to detect the amount of water present. The ESP32 microcontroller continuously reads the sensor val-ues. When the water level falls below the minimum level, the ESP32 turns ON the water pump through a relay module. The pump fills the tank with water. When the tank reaches the maximum level, the ESP32 automatically turns OFF the water pump The current wa-ter level and pump status are displayed on the LCD display. A buzzer provides alerts when the tank is empty or full. Using the built-in Wi-Fi of ESP32, the water level data is sent to an IoT platform such as Blynk. Users can monitor the tank level and pump status remotely through a smartphone. 1. System Overview The IoT-Based Water Tank Level Indicator automatically monitors the water level in an overhead tank and controls the water pump accordingly. It prevents water overflow and dry running of the pump while allowing users to monitor tank status remotely through the Internet. 2. Main Components ESP32 Microcontroller HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor Relay Module Water Pump Power Supply IoT Platform (e.g., Blynk) Water Tank 3. Working Principle Step 1: Water Level Detection The HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor is mounted at the top of the tank. It continu-ously sends ultrasonic waves toward the water surface and receives the reflected waves. The distance between the sensor and water surface is calculated using: From the mea-sured distance, the water level percentage is determined. Step 2: Data Processing The ESP32 receives the distance data from the ultrasonic sensor and compares it with prede-fined minimum and maximum water level limits. If water level falls below the minimum level (e.g., 20If water level reaches the maximum level (e.g., 90Step 3: Automatic Pump Control The ESP32 controls a relay module connected to the water pump. Low water
